{#- Route table per locale. A visitor reading /es/ must not be sent
    back into the English tree by the nav — the same broken promise the
    runtime text swap made before the Spanish URLs existed. -#}
{%- set isEs = (L == "es") %}
{%- set navWork = "/es/trabajo/" if isEs else "/work/" %}
{%- set navLab = "/es/lab/" if isEs else "/lab/" %}
{%- set navStudio = "/es/estudio/" if isEs else "/studio/" %}
{%- set navNotes = "/es/notas/" if isEs else "/insights/" %}
{%- set navServices = "/es/servicios/" if isEs else "/services/" %}
{#- Nav labels, resolved at build time. They used to be English in the markup
    on every page, with js/i18n.js swapping them after load — so the anchor
    text a crawler read on /es/servicios/ was "Work", "About", "Services".
    Anchor text is one of the few signals a crawler gets for free, and the
    Spanish tree was spending all of it on English words. -#}
{%- set labelWork = "Proyectos" if isEs else "Work" %}
{%- set labelServices = "Servicios" if isEs else "Services" %}
{%- set labelLab = "Lab" %}
{%- set labelAbout = "Nosotros" if isEs else "About" %}
{%- set labelNotes = "Insights" %}
{%- set labelContact = "Contacto" if isEs else "Contact" %}
{%- set labelAll = "Todas las capacidades" if isEs else "All Capabilities" %}
{#- Current-section tests, so wayfinding works on both trees. They match the
    section rather than one exact URL: a case page should light "Work", which
    the old equality test never did. -#}
{%- set atWork = ("/work/" in page.url) or ("/es/trabajo/" in page.url) %}
{%- set atLab = ("/lab/" in page.url) %}
{%- set atStudio = ("/studio/" in page.url) or ("/es/estudio/" in page.url) %}
{%- set atNotes = ("/insights/" in page.url) or ("/es/notas/" in page.url) %}
{%- set atServices = ("/services/" in page.url) or ("/es/servicios/" in page.url) %}
{#- The language control, as links wherever a real sibling URL exists.

    It was two <button>s. Buttons are not links: a crawler does not press them,
    so the entire Spanish tree had no crawlable path in from the English one —
    the audit found seventeen URLs reachable only through the sitemap. The JS
    handler in js/i18n.js already navigated to the sibling; the markup simply
    never told anyone but a mouse. An <a href> is the same gesture for a
    visitor, a real edge for a crawler, and middle-click-openable for the
    bilingual reader who wants both.

    Where a page genuinely has no sibling — /terms/ today — that side stays a
    button and keeps the in-place dictionary swap, which is the honest shape:
    there is no other document to point at. -#}
{%- set enHref = altEn if altEn else (canonical if L != "es" else "") %}
{%- set esHref = altEs if altEs else (canonical if L == "es" else "") %}
{%- macro langSwitch(id) %}
        <div class="lang-switch"{% if id %} id="{{ id }}"{% endif %}>
          {%- if enHref %}
          <a class="lang-switch__btn{{ " active" if L != "es" }}" href="{{ enHref }}" hreflang="en" data-lang="en" lang="en"{% if L != "es" %} aria-current="true"{% endif %} aria-label="Switch to English">EN</a>
          {%- else %}
          <button class="lang-switch__btn{{ " active" if L != "es" }}" type="button" data-lang="en" aria-label="Switch to English">EN</button>
          {%- endif %}
          {%- if esHref %}
          <a class="lang-switch__btn{{ " active" if L == "es" }}" href="{{ esHref }}" hreflang="es" data-lang="es" lang="es"{% if L == "es" %} aria-current="true"{% endif %} aria-label="Cambiar a Espa&ntilde;ol">ES</a>
          {%- else %}
          <button class="lang-switch__btn{{ " active" if L == "es" }}" type="button" data-lang="es" aria-label="Cambiar a Espa&ntilde;ol">ES</button>
          {%- endif %}
        </div>
{%- endmacro %}
{#- One header for the whole site. It used to exist in eight hand-maintained
    variants across three technologies, which is the economic reason the site
    stopped at six URLs: every new page meant another copy to keep in sync.

    Subpages pass `subpage: true` and get the frosted state plus the same
    navigation — before this, /work/ and /lab/ had no site nav at all, so a
    visitor who reached them could only go home or to the contact form. -#}
  <header class="header{% if subpage %} scrolled subpage__header{% endif %}" id="header">
    <div class="header__inner">
      {#- The logo was hardcoded to "/". On a Spanish page that is the one link
          every visitor trusts to mean "start over", and it dropped them into
          English — the same broken promise the nav table above exists to
          prevent. It has a Spanish front door to point at now. -#}
      <a href="{{ "/es/" if isEs else "/" }}" class="header__logo" aria-label="{{ "CREATIVE MK — Inicio" if isEs else "CREATIVE MK Home" }}">
        <span class="header__logo-mark">CREATIVE<span class="header__logo-mk">mk</span></span>
      </a>
      {#- Wayfinding (immersive-plan §12): the underline slides to the link
          whose section is on screen — one indicator, moved by js/daylight.js.
          The dropdown stops being furniture: each item opens its own
          accordion row via data-cap-index, or jumps to its real section. -#}
      <nav class="header__nav" id="main-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="{{ navWork }}" class="header__nav-link" data-nav-section="work"{% if atWork %} aria-current="page"{% endif %} data-i18n="nav.work">{{ labelWork }}</a>
        <div class="header__dropdown">
          <button class="header__dropdown-trigger" data-nav-section="capabilities"{% if atServices %} aria-current="true"{% endif %} aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="services-menu">
            <span data-i18n="nav.services">{{ labelServices }}</span>
            <svg class="header__dropdown-icon" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 4l4 4 4-4"/></svg>
          </button>
          {#- Was: seven links, five of which resolved to the SAME anchor
              (#capabilities) and merely opened an accordion row. Now each one
              is its own page. This is the mechanism the owner named when he
              said the site felt like a single landing page. -#}
          {#- On a Spanish page the dropdown points at the Spanish tree.
              Sending a visitor who is reading /es/servicios/ back into the
              English pages is the same broken promise as the runtime swap
              this replaced. -#}
          <div class="header__dropdown-menu">
            {%- for service in services %}
            {%- if L == "es" %}
            <a href="/es/servicios/{{ service.esSlug }}/" class="header__dropdown-item">{{ service.es.title }}</a>
            {%- else %}
            <a href="/services/{{ service.slug }}/" class="header__dropdown-item">{{ service.en.title }}</a>
            {%- endif %}
            {%- endfor %}
            <a href="{{ "/es/servicios/" if L == "es" else "/services/" }}" class="header__dropdown-item" data-i18n="nav.allServices">{{ labelAll }}</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href="{{ navLab }}" class="header__nav-link" data-nav-section="lab"{% if atLab %} aria-current="page"{% endif %} data-i18n="nav.lab">{{ labelLab }}</a>
        <a href="{{ navStudio }}" class="header__nav-link" data-nav-section="about"{% if atStudio %} aria-current="page"{% endif %} data-i18n="nav.about">{{ labelAbout }}</a>
        <a href="{{ navNotes }}" class="header__nav-link" data-nav-section="news"{% if atNotes %} aria-current="page"{% endif %} data-i18n="nav.blog">{{ labelNotes }}</a>
        <span class="header__nav-underline" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </nav>
      <div class="header__right">
        <button class="sound-toggle" id="sound-toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Ambient sound / Sonido ambiental">
          <span class="sound-toggle__bar"></span><span class="sound-toggle__bar"></span><span class="sound-toggle__bar"></span>
        </button>
{{ langSwitch("lang-switch") }}
        <a href="/contact" class="header__contact-btn" data-i18n="nav.contact">{{ "Contacto" if isEs else "Contact" }}</a>
      </div>
      <button class="header__menu-toggle" id="menu-toggle" aria-label="Toggle menu" aria-expanded="false">
        <span></span><span></span><span></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="header__rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <nav class="header__mobile-nav" id="mobile-nav" aria-label="Mobile navigation">
      <a href="{{ navWork }}" class="header__mobile-nav-link" data-i18n="nav.work">{{ labelWork }}</a>
      <a href="{{ navLab }}" class="header__mobile-nav-link" data-i18n="nav.lab">{{ labelLab }}</a>
      <a href="{{ navServices }}" class="header__mobile-nav-link" data-i18n="nav.services">{{ labelServices }}</a>
      <a href="{{ navStudio }}" class="header__mobile-nav-link" data-i18n="nav.about">{{ labelAbout }}</a>
      <a href="{{ navNotes }}" class="header__mobile-nav-link" data-i18n="nav.blog">{{ labelNotes }}</a>
      <a href="/contact" class="header__mobile-nav-link" data-i18n="nav.contact">{{ labelContact }}</a>
      <div class="lang-switch-wrap" style="margin-top:auto;">{{ langSwitch("") }}</div>
    </nav>
  </header>
